.TH CHTTPCLIENT_ASYNC_RESULT_GET 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpclient_async_result_get \- block until the future of an async request is fulfilled, then give its typed result
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

chttpcli_async_result_t *chttpclient_async_result_get(ctpool_future *f);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This is a thin wrapper over ctpool_future_get that casts its void*
result to chttpcli_async_result_t*. As with ctpool_future_get, you can
call it more than once on the same future: every later call returns the
same result pointer, which the future owns until it is freed.

The result has two public fields:
  - rv holds the code that chttpclient_do would return for the same
    request.
  - resp is not NULL only when rv == ccol_success. The caller then owns
    resp and frees it with chttpclient_resp_free before calling
    chttpclient_async_result_free.
A successful request from chttpclient_do_async_streaming fills resp as
well, and its status_code means the same thing. resp->body is NULL,
resp->body_len is 0 and resp->headers is NULL there, though, because
the write callback received the body and the client keeps no headers.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
f The future from chttpclient_do_async or from
  chttpclient_do_async_streaming.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
The result, or NULL if f is NULL or the future was cancelled before it
was fulfilled.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpclient_do_async (3),
.BR chttpclient_do_async_streaming (3),
.BR chttpclient_async_result_free (3),
.BR ctpool_future_get (3)
